course: dictionary
lesson: 10628
title: Unforeseen: not expected
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Due to unforeseen circumstances, the trip is cancelled.» Unforeseen means not expected or planned for. Break the word into parts: un means not, fore means before, and seen means seen. So something unforeseen was not seen coming beforehand.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The trip is cancelled, and the reason is «unforeseen circumstances», which means things nobody planned for. You do not need the exact reason to know the trip could not go ahead because of something nobody expected.
explain: In old writing you may meet «fleet and unforeseen», which means fast and unexpected. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "fast and not expected" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Unforeseen means not expected or planned for; nobody guessed it would happen.
fact: Common phrases with unforeseen are «unforeseen circumstances», «unforeseen problems» and «unforeseen costs».
fact: Unforeseen costs are extra costs you did not plan for, such as a bike puncture on a family trip.
fact: Notices and formal letters use unforeseen to explain a change without giving every detail.
fact: Unforeseen is close in meaning to unexpected: both describe something you did not think would happen.
exercise: «Due to unforeseen circumstances, the trip is cancelled.» What does unforeseen mean? | *Not expected or planned for | Happening every week | Written down in advance | Very expensive
exercise: Mum says the budget had unforeseen costs. What are unforeseen costs? | Costs you planned for carefully | *Extra costs you did not plan for | Costs that are paid back the next day
exercise: Which phrase means problems nobody expected? | *unforeseen problems | planned trips | sunny weather
test: In old writing, «fleet and unforeseen» means fast and what? | *unexpected | slow | planned
test: Un means not, fore means before, and seen means seen. So unforeseen means what? | seen again twice | seen clearly from far away | *not seen coming beforehand
exam: The school trip was cancelled because of unforeseen problems. Which word could replace unforeseen without changing the meaning? | famished | ancient | planned | *unexpected
